{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENPY2FuEH87xBeGW1eY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed both bugs, and they had the same cause: `src/app.py` used `hidden`, a DynamoDB reserved word, as a bare attribute name. All 12 tests pass; I've only run them locally against the in-repo fake, not against real DynamoDB.\n\n**Causes (also in `ANSWER.md`):**\n1. **Prod crash:** `hide()` sent `SET hidden = :h`. DynamoDB rejects a bare reserved word in an update, so every Hide click raised a `ValidationException` and returned a 500. No story could be hidden through the API.\n2. **Staging feed:** Dasha's hand-made update did write the flag. The problem was on the read side: `feed()` listed `hidden` bare in its `ProjectionExpression`, so the field came back missing with no error. The \"not hidden\" check was therefore always true and the filter never removed anything. It wasn't caching and it wasn't a different table.\n\nThe old tests missed both: none of them called `hide()` or ever set `hidden` on a story.\n\n**One thing doesn't add up.** The guide and the repo's fake both say a bare reserved word in a projection just drops the field silently. AWS's own docs say it's rejected with the same error as the update. If that's how staging behaved, `/feed` would have returned a 500, not the 200 in the report. Either way the cause in the code and the fix are the same. I noted this in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **Aliases everywhere:** every attribute name in every expression in `src/app.py` now goes through a `#alias` (`#hid` → `hidden`, and so on), whether or not the word is reserved today. Method names and signatures are unchanged, so the handlers in the infra repo don't need changes.\n- **Guard so it can't come back:** the tests now run against a stricter fake table that rejects *any* bare attribute name in any expression. A future field can't slip in un-aliased, even if it isn't on today's reserved list.\n- **Tests with the field actually set:** hiding through `hide()`, hiding by hand the way staging did, hiding a story that doesn't exist, archiving, feed paging, and two tests that pin the fake's reserved-word behaviour.\n- **Checked against the old code:** run on the old `app.py`, the new tests reproduce both reported failures: the `hidden` error and the hand-hidden story still in the feed.\n\n**Two more bugs I found and fixed:**\n- **`archive()`:** it used `status` bare, which is also reserved. It would have crashed the first time the admin console called it.\n- **Feed paging:** `feed()` only read the first page of results (DynamoDB returns at most 1 MB per call). Once the table grew, stories past that page would have silently dropped out of the feed. It now reads every page.\n\nNothing is committed or deployed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1449,"cache_read_input_tokens":34133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1449},"output_tokens":714,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f973ea9-0859-4276-b508-9084dafb7305","uuid":"12e27416-1024-4bc2-80e7-54e2438a09c8","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:38:14.263Z","request_id":"req_011CgENPXjea9b67TkWqj9JQ"}
